501:  resize() {

Good, resize is called on init. Add fit logic in resize. But if the user orbits and the window resizes, it resets. Acceptable.

Implement:
```
resize() {
  ...
  this.camera.aspect = ...
  this.camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
  const portrait = this.camera.aspect < 0.82;
  const targetZ = portrait ? 4.75 : 3.5;
  if (this.camera.position.length() > 0) { ... } // set only if not user-adjusted
  ...
}
```
We need to preserve orbit direction when fitting? On mobile initial load, camera at (0,0.12,3.5). Setting z=4.75 fine. If the user has orbited, resetting is jarring. Add `this.hasInteracted = false` and `controls.addEventListener('start', () => this.hasInteracted = true)`. Then in resize, if `!this.hasInteracted`, set camera. If interacted, keep. Good.

Add in constructor after controls setup:
```
this.hasInteracted = false;
this.controls.addEventListener('start', () => { this.hasInteracted = true; });
```
But OrbitControls 'start' fires on pointer down; zoom/scroll also. Good.

In resize:
```
if (!this.hasInteracted) {
  const portrait = this.camera.aspect < 0.82;
  this.camera.position.set(0, portrait ? 0.16 : 0.12, portrait ? 4.85 : 3.5);
  this.controls.target.set(0, portrait ? 0.04 : 0.02, 0);
  this.controls.update();
}
```
Also `resetView()` should set hasInteracted=false? It sets the camera; yes, set false then fit.

Update resetView to use aspect and same distances.

Let's edit.

